    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d229">

                <pb facs="0320" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6131/330: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-07-13T13:00:00+03:00">July 13, 1935—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 13—6:34 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>281. I signed today at 1 o’clock with Litvinov notes and letters and will release
                    notes to press at 5 p.m., this afternoon, Saturday July 13th (10 a.m.,
                    Washington time). I venture to suggest that in issuing the text of the identic
                    notes the Department should at the same time make the statement made in the
                    fifth paragraph of my 275, July 11, 5 p.m. I will make available to the press on
                    July 15, 5 p.m. (10 a.m. Washington time) the text of my letter to Litvinov
                    dated July 11 and of Litvinov’s reply dated July 15th.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
